            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous recovery of an aqueductal stenosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>231-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The case of a 17-year-old male with hydrocephalus caused by aqueductal obstruction is presented. A ventriculo-peritoneal shunt was implanted and later removed due to an infection. In the clinical follow-up no deterioration was observed. No further surgery was necessary. The repeat-MRI showed spontaneous resolution of the hydrocephalus with a normal aqueduct.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
